odot/pulls/124033","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124033","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124033.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124033.patch","merged_at":"2026-09-30T19:43:03Z"},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\n`Ref<T>::instantiate()` was operating slightly less optimally than intended, as it wasn't properly forwarding its variadic arguments. This PR rectifies that issue by ensuring the template passes with forwarding references (`&&`) & utilizes `std::forward` during construction. I'm not positive if this was impacting us to any measurable extent, but this forwarding variadic implementation is already used elsewhere in the repo, which I believe alone validates the integration\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\nIncludes a minor stylistic change: renaming `VarArgs` to `Args` for the variadic template types. The former is meant for contexts where items are convertible `Variant` (`varray`, `sarray`, etc.), while `Args` is generally our naming scheme for unconstrained variadic arguments","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_t